   "skip": [
    "streettexture.dds"
   ],
   "skipComment": "`streettexture.dds` and `streettexture.jpg` share a stem, so both would be the asset `streettexture/streettexture`. The runner builds one asset per `BuildContent` call with `RebuildAll`, so it never saw a collision -- it simply wrote the second over the first, and its loop is sorted ordinal-ignore-case, which puts `.dds` first and lets `.jpg` win. The corpus agrees: the reference is 1,048,763 bytes, which is 512x512 in `Color` and not a compressed surface. A single project cannot express 'build both, keep the last', so the loser is skipped by name."
